Diagnostic tables
=================

This directory holds the source tables for every diagnostic code the Kairo
compiler emits. The code scheme, the table format, the registry, rendering
and clang mapping are specified in Compiler/Spec/Diagnostics.md.

Files

  <Category>.diag.toml   one table per category: Syntax (S), Resolution (R),
                         Semantic (SC), Lowering (CL), Memory (M), Linker (L),
                         Portability (P), Optimization (OPT), Internal (I),
                         Uncategorized (U). Edit these by hand.
  Clang.diag.toml        C codes for clang warning groups. Generated; do not
                         edit.
  ClangDiagCodes.toml    the persistent allocation manifest behind
                         Clang.diag.toml. Never renumber or delete entries.

Generated from these files (never edit by hand):

  Compiler/Diagnostic/Registry.k          by Scripts/gen_diag.py
  Compiler/Diagnostic/ClangDiagLookup.k   by Scripts/gen_clang_diag_table.py

Regenerating

The clang table first, since gen_diag.py reads its output (only needed when
the clang version changes):

  ./build/x86_64-linux-gnu/debug/bin/clang-diag-identity \
      | python3 Scripts/gen_clang_diag_table.py \
          --manifest Compiler/Diagnostic/TableGen/ClangDiagCodes.toml \
          --output Compiler/Diagnostic/TableGen/Clang.diag.toml \
          --lookup-output Compiler/Diagnostic/ClangDiagLookup.k

Then the registry. build.py's prebuild step runs this on every build, so by
hand it is only needed to inspect the output:

  python3 Scripts/gen_diag.py Compiler/Diagnostic/TableGen \
      --output=Compiler/Diagnostic/Registry.k \
      --full-output=build/registry/Compiler/Diagnostic/Registry.k

Compiler/Diagnostic/Registry.k carries the declarations the tree imports;
build/registry/ holds declarations plus bodies, which each build compiles into
its own registry object (<out>/obj/registry/registry.o, see build.py
gen_registry / selfhost_registry). Both are rewritten only when their text
changes, so an edited table needs nothing beyond a rebuild; the object is also
recompiled when a module it imports changes (selfhost_registry keys on them).

That object is linked into EVERY tool build.py makes, including ones whose
graph never reaches the compiler (kld, katar, clang-diag-identity), and it is
compiled --emit-scope=inputs. So it must be self-contained: it may reference
no symbol of a compiler module, only types and inline bodies. That is why
diag_from_string's hash is written out by gen_diag.py (constants from
Scripts/Migration/eval_hash.py) instead of calling Support/EvalHash.k's
compute_hash. Check with `llvm-nm -u -C <out>/obj/registry/registry.o`.
